Before changing the public front-end, read:

- `doc/architecture/frontend/brand-and-ux-system.md`
- `doc/architecture/frontend/landing-and-player-ux.md`
- `doc/architecture/frontend/wow-content-integration.md`

Non-negotiable constraints:

- Product name is **M+ Trust Factor**; published metric is **Trust Score**; short mark is **M+TS**.
- Public skill dimensions are exactly four: Performance, Survival, Utility, Experience.
- Keep the visual balance approximately 75% modern SaaS/data and 25% Warcraft atmosphere.
- Use `apps/web/src/design-tokens.css`; do not introduce a second brand token file.
- Inter is the product font, Cinzel is a rare display accent, JetBrains Mono is for data values.
- Preserve route behavior and existing E2E `data-testid` values unless tests change in the same work.
- Blizzard is the source of truth for character, equipment, talent and media data.
- Wowhead is optional and presentation-only: documented tooltips and outbound links.
- Never scrape Wowhead, embed its model viewer or depend on undocumented private endpoints.
- Core profile and equipment UI must work when all third-party scripts are blocked.
- Show confidence, freshness and methodology near the score.
- Design loading, partial, unavailable, stale and failure states.
- Maintain keyboard access, reduced-motion support and a text equivalent for charts.
